  "prefLabel": "Ed 1019.21 Administrative Reviews, Evidentiary Hearings, and Arbitration of Manager Complaints",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ed 1019.21 Administrative Reviews, Evidentiary Hearings, and Arbitration of Manager Complaints. If a manager or the committee is aggrieved by any action of SBVI with regard to the administration of the program, the manager, the committee, or the aggrieved individual may file a written complaint to resolve the matter in accordance with Ed 200. If the matter is not resolved to the satisfaction of the complainant at the conclusion of the process outlined in Ed 200, the complainant may appeal the decision under 34 CFR 395.13 and 34 CFR 395.37.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note #1, #2, and #3 at chapter heading for Ed 1000) #13231, eff 7-13-21",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ed1000.html"
